# What a local `docker build` from the repo root must not send (#396).
#
# The Dockerfiles copy `shared/`, `services/…` and `dashboard/` whole, so anything
# lying in the working tree went into the image: a community all-in-one image built
# after `npm run build` contained services/billing-bridge/dist and started it; dist
# files tsc no longer emits survived; Windows-built Prisma engines landed in a Linux
# image. The image builds everything it needs itself. CI never noticed — a clean
# checkout has none of this.

# Installed and built output — the image installs and builds its own.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Secrets and local state.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.log

# Repository and tooling metadata.
.git
.github
.claude
**/.vscode
**/.idea
graphify-out
